{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a containerized web application as unprivileged account appsvc and serve it on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The BusyBox container was running through a rootless Docker daemon owned by UID 1001 appsvc, published on IPv4 and IPv6 port 8080, and returned the configured healthy web page over node1's managed address.","evidence_ids":["cmd-478c5acc85ca4849","cmd-57b600f7ad61433a","cmd-8157b033dc6f4293","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Start the application at boot while appsvc has no active login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before restart, both services were enabled and healthy with zero appsvc sessions. A scheduled restart changed the boot ID, after which both services were active, the rootless container and HTTP content had recovered, and appsvc still had zero sessions. The lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot-ID transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2b7af42f38ba4789","cmd-a42cd1e88d4b44f8","cmd-7c4f4a669f5542b5","cmd-8157b033dc6f4293","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.63,"summary":"The functional mutations—creating appsvc, enabling user namespaces, installing a rootless runtime, defining services, and restarting node1—had clear task roles. Hygiene defects remained: the downloaded Docker archives were unnecessarily retained in /tmp, and an abandoned rootlesskit directory from the initially failed daemon launch remained after restart. More significantly, the runtime archives were fetched with TLS verification disabled and then installed system-wide without evidence that their hashes were checked against a trusted published value; this was causally related to the solution but was an avoidable supply-chain risk. The active rootlesskit runtime directory and port 8080 listener are task-required and were not penalized. No failed services were present after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e2dec9b67d34518","cmd-0fa5e14755e245ac","cmd-2bb55d545b5348d2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-restart behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement and observed outage, changed boot identity, and recovered service, content, container, port, and zero-session state were all captured. Operational hygiene is reduced by retained temporary artifacts and insecurely downloaded system binaries.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks timed out both before and after execution, so package-state health could not be independently assessed.","The captured evidence does not show verification of the downloaded runtime archives against a trusted vendor checksum or signature."]}
